<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=galvanization">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Chemistry</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galvanisation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">by the 1680s</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as galvanisation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galvanisation is the process of applying a protective zinc coating to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> or iron to prevent rusting, most often by dipping parts in a bath of molten zinc. The earliest known galvanised iron is on an Indian armour in the Royal Armouries Museum collection in the United Kingdom, known from its inscriptions to be earlier than the 1680s. The process is named after the Italian physician Luigi Galvani (1737–1798). Galvanic paint, a precursor to hot-dip galvanising, was patented by Stanislas Sorel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 10 June 1837. In the early twentieth century galvanised piping replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cast-iron">cast iron</a> and lead in cold-water plumbing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galvanization.jpg" alt="Galvanisation" width="330" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TMg · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Feuerverzinktes_Geländer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>by the 1680s</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>India</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Stanislas Sorel</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Galvanic paint, a precursor to hot-dip galvanising, was patented by Stanislas Sorel of Paris on 10 June 1837, the date most often associated with the process.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/iron-smelting">Iron smelting<span>c. 2500 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=galvanization">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
